# CSS in dev (Nitro SSR)

When Nitro owns SSR, Vite’s module graph is a different realm (`globalThis.__viteDevServer` is missing). Layout/page CSS modules hash class names on the server but rules are not in the HTML unless injected.

- Dev: `<link rel="stylesheet" href="…file.module.css?direct">` so Vite returns `text/css` with hashed names.
- Do not use `?inline` (skips module hashing). Do not use deferred module scripts (FOUC).
- `collectCssFromModuleGraph` is for Avalon’s own SSR middleware, not the Nitro runner.
- Production: import layout CSS from the client entry (default import, not side-effect) and `injectAssets` from the client manifest.
- New CSS files: discovery runs at plugin load — restart the dev server.

See `generateLayoutsModule` in `nitro-integration.ts` and `collect-css.ts`.
